    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8f47b043-9bc7-55d4-8113-5becf03d9d90",
      ":question/problem": "What is $\\displaystyle \\int(x^{2} - \\sqrt{x} + 2)dx$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(x^{2}-\\sqrt{x}+2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(x^{2}-x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-\\int x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+2\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{x^{2+1}}{(2+1)}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{1}{2}+1}}{(\\frac{1}{2}+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +2\\left(\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{x^{3}}{3}-\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{3}+2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
