    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cdf1a383-5fd9-556f-8c2f-00f45613294e",
      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$4x^{7} + \\sqrt[5]{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{13}}}$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(4x^{7}+\\sqrt[5]{x}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{13}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(4x^{7}+x^{\\frac{1}{5}}-x^{\\frac{-13}{7}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 4\\int x^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{\\frac{1}{5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-\\int x^{\\frac{-13}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 4\\left(\\frac{x^{7+1}}{(7+1)}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{1}{5}+1}}{(\\frac{1}{5}+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad -\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-13}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{-13}{7}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{x^{8}}{2}+\\frac{5\\sqrt[5]{x^{6}}}{6}+\\frac{7}{6\\sqrt[7]{x^{6}}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
